From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jbevan <jbevan@bu.edu>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:49:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Server: send the depth indicator as 16 bits

The depth indicator was a signed byte (TINY), which wraps in the far
wilderness. Sent as NORMAL (16 bits) instead. This changes what the server
sends: a client must have the same indicator table (the patched client
does; the tables are shared source).
---
 src/server/tables.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/server/tables.c b/src/server/tables.c
index 1a002012f1398c4e393a6ba4fa9917f7b338a143..7136464b171c6fa707a72dc7b7240f9c5b373500 100644
--- a/src/server/tables.c
+++ b/src/server/tables.c
@@ -770,7 +770,9 @@ const indicator_type indicators[MAX_INDICATORS] =
 		(PR_STUDY),  "study"
 	},
 	{
-		INDICATOR_PKT(DEPTH, TINY, 1),   	IPW_2,	ROW_DEPTH, COL_DEPTH,
+		/* NORMAL (16 bits), not TINY: a signed byte wraps in the far
+		 * wilderness (test-server change; the Advisor's game-state survey) */
+		INDICATOR_PKT(DEPTH, NORMAL, 1),   	IPW_2,	ROW_DEPTH, COL_DEPTH,
 		(0),
 		"Lev \aw%3d",
 		(PR_DEPTH),  "depth"
